@startuml Amdox-ERP-BullMQ
title Amdox ERP — Async Job Queue (BullMQ) Sequence

' What this shows: how a slow / unreliable task (like calling an external
' webhook) is handled WITHOUT blocking the user's request. The API just drops
' a job on the queue and responds; a worker does the real work later and
' retries automatically if it fails.

actor User
participant "Backend API\n(Express)" as API
participant "Service" as SVC
queue "Redis\n(BullMQ queue)" as Q
participant "Worker\n(runs in backend)" as W
participant "External\nWebhook URL" as EXT
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

User -> API : record payment
API -> SVC : paymentService.create()
SVC -> DB : INSERT payment (in transaction)
SVC -> Q : enqueue 'webhook' job\n(non-blocking, ~5ms)
API --> User : 200 OK (instant)

== later, in the background ==

W -> Q : pull next job
W -> EXT : POST signed payload
EXT --> W : HTTP 500 (fails)
W -> DB : log delivery attempt
note over W, Q
  attempt 1 failed -> BullMQ re-queues
  with exponential backoff (3s, 6s...)
end note

W -> Q : pull job again (attempt 2)
W -> EXT : POST payload
EXT --> W : HTTP 500 (fails)
W -> Q : pull job again (attempt 3)
W -> EXT : POST payload
EXT --> W : HTTP 500 (fails)
note over W
  after 3 attempts -> job moves to
  "failed". Visible in Bull Board
  at /api/admin/queues.
end note
@enduml
